---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { siteOperator, siteUrl } from '../lib/site-operator';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for OpenSkies."
>
  <p>
    This policy describes how I handle information when you visit
    <a href={siteUrl}>{siteUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>. I operate OpenSkies
    as an individual. I do not offer user accounts, newsletters, or forms that
    collect personal data on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    I’m responsible for data processing on this site. For
    privacy questions, contact me at
    <a href={`mailto:${siteOperator.email}`}>{siteOperator.email}</a>. See all contact details on the
    <a href="/imprint">imprint</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>What I process</h2>
  <p>
    When you open pages or download photos, my hosting and content delivery
    providers process technical data needed to deliver the site, such as your IP
    address, browser type, requested URL, and time of access. This happens
    automatically in the server and CDN logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    I do not ask you to register, and I do not knowingly collect names, email
    addresses, or other information you enter on OpenSkies, because the site
    does not provide those features.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and CDN</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on Cloudflare. Photos are stored and delivered via
    Cloudflare at cdn.openskies.photos. Cloudflare processes
    technical data as my processor to provide hosting, security, and
    delivery. For more information, see
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    I do not use analytics or advertising cookies on OpenSkies. The gallery may
    update the page URL in your browser (for example when you filter by color or
    open a photo) without storing a profile about you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare or your browser may set strictly necessary cookies or use local
    storage for security or basic operation of the network; I do not use these to
    track you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>Why I process data</h2>
  <p>
    I rely on my legitimate interest in operating a stable, secure public website
    and delivering the photos you request (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object to
    processing based on legitimate interests by contacting me; I will weigh your
    interests against mine.
  </p>

  <h2>How long I keep data</h2>
  <p>
    Access logs at my providers are kept only as long as needed for operations,
    security, and troubleshooting, according to their retention practices, then
    deleted or aggregated.
  </p>

  <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare may process data in countries outside the European Economic Area.
    Where required, appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses)
    apply as described by Cloudflare.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    If GDPR applies to you, you have the right to access, rectify, erase, or
    restrict processing of personal data I hold about you, to object to certain
    processing, and to data portability where applicable. You may also lodge a
    complaint with a supervisory authority. In Germany, you can contact the
    authority responsible for your place of residence; for Hamburg, that is the
    <a href="https://datenschutz-hamburg.de/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hamburg Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    I may update this policy when the site or legal requirements change. The
    current version is always published on this page.
  </p>
  <p><em>Last updated: May 2026</em></p>
</ProseLayout>
